WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.480
Let me draw a random polygon.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.700
A polygon is a closed figure with three or more sides.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.520
And we have another polygon here.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.040
Are these two figures congruent?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.800
Well, they look like each other.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.380
But the condition for congruency says that

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.520
these two figures are congruent if one when placed on the other,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.360
they both should overlap exactly.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.160
If we move this one over the first one,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.220
we can see that it overlaps exactly.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.440
It means they are congruent figures.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.680
Let's erase this and draw another polygon.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.740
And here's another one.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.220
Are these two figures congruent.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.620
At first, they don't look congruent, but that's the trick.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.360
This polygon when placed on this one, overlaps exactly.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.740
So they are congruent too.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.860
Doesn't matter how they are placed that's congruency.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.620
But let's understand a bit more about congruency.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.260
When are two figures congruent?

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:07.580
It's simple!

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.320
They should have the same shape,

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.160
as well as the same size.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.680
Say we have a shape like this.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.900
And another one like this.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.940
We can easily say that they are not congruent

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.860
as they're completely different shapes.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.400
Now look at this shape and this one.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.360
We can see that their shape is the same.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:32.920
But wait, the sizes are different.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.380
Which is why these two figures are also not congruent.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.920
But what about these two shapes?

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.740
They have the same shape as well as the same size.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.960
They are congruent figures!

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.480
But we cannot place a figure on the other

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.480
to know if they are congruent or not.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.220
So how can we say if two figures are congruent or not?

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.140
We need to understand a simple concept first!

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.420
Is it only figures that can be congruent.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.800
Consider two segments. Segment AB and segment CD.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.340
Both measure 3 units.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.380
Can we say that they are congruent? Of course we can.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.600
Segment AB is congruent to segment CD.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:23.640
What if we have two angles like this with the same measure?

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.420
Say both measure 60 degrees.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.600
Yes, these two angles are also congruent.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.440
Coming back to our question, when are two figures congruent?

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.720
Look at these two triangles

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.900
When can we say that they are congruent?

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.380
We can say that these two triangles are congruent

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:50.140
if all the matching sides and all the matching angles are congruent!

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:53.280
We will understand more about congruence of triangles

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.540
in the coming videos.

